  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 28f310e05cc019a48855581da30b411e, type: 3}
  m_Name: DinuguanHistory
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  lines:
  - text: Dark, rich, and unapologetically Filipino.
    characterSprite: {fileID: -8056027616224820867, guid: 783feefcd5809a142b7b39ffbbe1c917, type: 3}
  - text: "Some call it \u201Cchocolate meat\u201D when introducing it kindly to a visitor,"
    characterSprite: {fileID: -8056027616224820867, guid: 783feefcd5809a142b7b39ffbbe1c917, type: 3}
  - text: 'but this dish is proud of what it is. Its roots run deep into pre colonial feasting, '
    characterSprite: {fileID: -8056027616224820867, guid: 783feefcd5809a142b7b39ffbbe1c917, type: 3}
  - text: 'where the whole animal was honored and nothing went to waste. '
    characterSprite: {fileID: -8056027616224820867, guid: 783feefcd5809a142b7b39ffbbe1c917, type: 3}
  - text: Pigafetta himself wrote about Filipinos preparing pork and blood together as early as 1521.
    characterSprite: {fileID: -8056027616224820867, guid: 783feefcd5809a142b7b39ffbbe1c917, type: 3}
  - text: 'Can you balance the vinegar, the aromatics, '
    characterSprite: {fileID: -8056027616224820867, guid: 783feefcd5809a142b7b39ffbbe1c917, type: 3}
  - text: and the offal to earn this dish its honored place on your table?
    characterSprite: {fileID: -8056027616224820867, guid: 783feefcd5809a142b7b39ffbbe1c917, type: 3}
